```

List the problems, then refactor:

```js
var d = [];
function proc(x) {
  for (var i = 0; i < x.length; i++) {
    if (x[i].s == 1) {
      d.push(x[i]);
    }
  }
  return d;
}
```

answer:
Problems: `d` is a global mutable accumulator that is never reset, so a second call returns results from both calls; `var` instead of `const`/`let`; loose `==`; magic number `1`; meaningless names (`d`, `proc`, `x`, `s`). Refactor:

```js
const STATUS_ACTIVE = 1;
function activeItems(items) {
  return items.filter(item => item.status === STATUS_ACTIVE);
}
```
